# Records Retention Schedule — <ENTITY NAME>

**Adopted:** <YYYY-MM-DD> · **Records custodian:** <NAME, OFFICE>

Two columns, deliberately. The **legal floor** is what a statute or regulation requires and is not
a matter of preference. The **entity policy** may be longer, and usually should be for anything
that establishes basis, authority, or a position that stays open.

| Record class | Legal floor | Source of the floor | Entity policy | Destruction authority |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Charter, amendments, bylaws, minutes, consents, stock records | While the entity exists and after dissolution as the formation state requires | <STATE STATUTE — verify> | Permanent | Board resolution only |
| Filed returns and acceptance evidence | While material under §6001, and at least until the assessment period closes | §6001; §6501 | Permanent | Board resolution only |
| Books, ledgers, and the records behind a return | While material under §6001 | §6001; Reg. §1.6001-1 | 7 years after the return's period closes | Custodian |
| Basis records (shares, contributed property, fixed assets) | As long as the contents may become material — ordinarily through the limitations period for the return on which the basis is used | §6001; Reg. §1.6001-1(e); §6501 | Permanent | Custodian |
| Employment tax records | 4 years after the tax becomes due or is paid, whichever is later | Reg. §31.6001-1 | 7 years | Custodian |
| Filed information returns, and data sufficient to reconstruct them | Generally at least 3 years from the due date; **4 years for Form 1099-C**; verify the form-specific rule | Current General Instructions for Certain Information Returns | 7 years | Custodian |
| Forms W-9 | 4 years after the last payment to that payee | Current Requester Instructions for Form W-9 | 7 years | Custodian |
| Forms W-8 and supporting documentation | As long as the form may be relevant to the withholding agent's liability under §§1461/1474 — apply the current form-specific validity and retention rules, which can run longer than four years | Current Requester Instructions for Forms W-8 | Longer of the legal floor and 7 years | Custodian |
| Accountable-plan claims, receipts, logs, and reconciliations | 4 years after the related employment tax is due or paid | Reg. §31.6001-1 | Retain with the annual workpaper set | Custodian |
| Bank and brokerage statements, and account-opening records | — | — | Permanent for opening records; 7 years for statements | Custodian |
| Contracts and their performance records | — | State limitations period | 7 years after the last obligation ends | Custodian |
| Correspondence with any taxing or licensing authority | — | — | Permanent | Board resolution only |
| Insurance policies | — | — | Permanent for occurrence policies | Custodian |

**Litigation and audit hold.** All destruction stops for any record class touched by a threatened
or pending examination, dispute, or proceeding, on written notice from <ROLE>, and resumes only on
written release.

**Format.** Records may be kept electronically where they remain complete, legible, and retrievable
for the full period, with the entity able to produce them in a readable form on request.

**Verify before relying.** Statutory citations and periods change; check each floor against current
law and the formation state's statute before the first destruction under this schedule.
